            "type": "callout",
            "tone": "definition",
            "title": "Scalars",
            "text": "Scalars are physical quantities that are described solely by a magnitude (size or amount) without any mention of direction. Thus scalars are directionless and can be fully characterised by a single number and its associated unit."
          },
          {
